    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d528-a2">

                <pb facs="0898" n="828" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg828"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 168.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Aarifi Pasha to Mr. Wallace.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Sublime Porte</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-01-27"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 27,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I received the note which your excellency
                    was good enough to address to me on the 25th of this month, No. 144, relative to
                    the complaint made by the reverend father, Mr. Cole, an American citizen, living
                    at Erzingan, against some Armenians.</p>
                <p>The necessary communications were immediately sent by telegraph to the imperial
                    authorities of the vilayet of Erzroom. I shall not fail to inform your
                    excellency of their reply as soon as it is received.</p>
                <p>I avail, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>A. AARIFI.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
